.TH AILAB 1 "2026" "ailab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ailab \- manage LXD-based sandboxes for running AI tools safely on Ubuntu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ailab
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ailab
creates lightweight LXD containers pre-wired to use AI services running
on the host (lemonade-server, ollama). Each container gets its own isolated
home directory, keeping installed software and the files an agent touches
separate from the rest of the system. All containers live in a dedicated
LXD project named \fBailab\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check that the environment is ready: LXD installed, initialised, and
reachable, and whether host AI services (lemonade-server, ollama) are
available. Reports a remedy for each problem found.
.TP
.B new \fINAME\fR [\-\-install \fIPACKAGE\fR] [\-\-port \fIHOST:CONTAINER\fR]
Create a new sandbox container. Optionally install one or more packages
immediately after creation; packages with an onboard step run it
automatically, then an interactive shell is opened.
.TP
.B run \fINAME\fR
Start the container (if stopped) and open an interactive login shell.
Alias: \fBshell\fR
.TP
.B info \fINAME\fR
Show a container's status, IP address, mapped user, config directory,
forwarded ports, and installed packages (when running).
.TP
.B logs \fINAME\fR [\-\-follow] [\-\-lines \fIN\fR]
Show the container's system journal. With \fB\-\-follow\fR (\fB\-f\fR),
stream new log lines until interrupted.
.TP
.B stop \fINAME\fR
Stop a running container.
.TP
.B list
List all ailab containers with status, IP address, and forwarded ports.
Alias: \fBls\fR
.TP
.B delete \fINAME\fR [\-\-force]
Stop and permanently delete a container. Prompts for confirmation unless
\fB\-\-force\fR is given.
Alias: \fBrm\fR
.TP
.B install \fINAME PACKAGE\fR
Install a pre-configured AI tool into an existing container. Tools are
configured for local-first AI with cloud providers disabled.
.TP
.B packages
List available installable packages from the app catalog.
Alias: \fBpkgs\fR
.TP
.B web \fR[\-\-host \fIHOST\fR] [\-\-port \fIPORT\fR]
Start the web management interface (binds 127.0.0.1:11500 by default).
.TP
.B dashboard
Print the web dashboard URL including its access token. Under the snap the
token file is root-owned: use \fBsudo ailab dashboard\fR.
.TP
.B port add \fINAME PORT\fR [\fICONTAINER_PORT\fR] [\-\-inbound]
Add a port proxy to a container. Default: outbound (host browser to
container service). With \fB\-\-inbound\fR: container localhost to host service.
.TP
.B port remove \fINAME PORT\fR
Remove a custom port proxy.
.TP
.B port list \fINAME\fR
List all port proxies on a container.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check the environment before creating a sandbox:
.B ailab doctor
.TP
Create a sandbox with openclaw, run onboarding, drop to shell:
.B ailab new mybox \-\-install openclaw
.TP
List all sandboxes:
.B ailab list
.TP
Open a shell in an existing sandbox:
.B ailab run mybox
.TP
Stop a running sandbox:
.B ailab stop mybox
.TP
Install nullclaw into an existing sandbox:
.B ailab install mybox nullclaw
.TP
Expose a port from the container to the host:
.B ailab port add mybox 9000
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/ailab/NAME/
Isolated per-container home directory (non-snap installs), bind-mounted as
the user's home path inside the container.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ailab/web-token
Web API access token (non-snap installs; under the snap it lives in the
snap's data directory). Printed by \fBailab dashboard\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lxc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Ken VanDine and contributors.
Homepage: https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/ailab
